[[4,3,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>1. Remove the piston rings.</p><p>2. Release the pin (2a) and separate the connecting rod (2b) from the piston (2c).</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/946000305.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[4,3,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>- Join the connecting rod and piston.</p><p>- Refit the pin in its seat and secure with new piston rings.</p>"],[2,3,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>1. Remove the piston rings.</p><p>2. Release the pin (2a) and separate the connecting rods (2b) from the pistons (2c).</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/939002424.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[2,3,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>1. Join the connecting rods to the pistons so that the number printed on the connecting rod head (1a) is facing notch (1b) on the piston skirt for the oil jet housing.</p><p>Fit the pins and secure them using the circlips.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/939002425.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[1,3,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>1. Remove the piston rings.</p><p>2. Release the pin (2a) and separate the connecting rod (2b) from the piston (2c).</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/939003517.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[1,3,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>- Join the connecting rod and piston.</p><p>- Place the gudgeon pin in its housings and secure it using the circlips.</p>"]]